WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.470
This is Milan's 'Porta Ticinese' district.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.020
It's home to many historic buildings.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.870
But some of the streets have drab architecture,
dating from the 1950s.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.130
They were eyesores, still

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:20.760
Giovanna Cornelio wanted to move into the
8th floor of  this building.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.540
She transformed into a luxurious living space.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.369
“Hello, nice to meet you.

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:28.630
Come in my home."

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:32.590
Inside it's anything but dull and dreary.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:36.500
The open-plan living room is flooded with
light.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:42.410
Cornelio turned two apartments into one and
now has 280 square meters of floor space.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:46.840
She's not bothered that the building's exterior
isn't so appealing.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.010
“I choose this house because of the light,
because of the terrace.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:57.330
I decide to draw this space according to the light during the day.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:07.930
So, every room has a different view outside and a different proportion with the light.”

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:11.400
Giovanna Cornelio loves '50s-era design.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.790
These eye-catching chairs are upholstered with fabric used to cover old train seats.

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:20.560
And this Jean Prouvé swing-arm lamp is also a design classic from 1950.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.670
The couch dates from the same era.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:31.310
“You can use it from this side, or you can
sit on the other side and look in this direction,

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:34.490
or have a sort of day bed.”

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:40.920
The architect designed some of the furniture herself, including this oversized couch and....

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.900
the shelving unit across from it.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:48.880
The kitchen is located on the same floor.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:54.460
Cornelio employed plenty of stainless steel, to make her kitchen durable and functional.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:58.820
"A simple design, but with strong materials to use every day.”

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:04.460
Across from the kitchen, the family meets
for meals.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:08.130
The architect has a 13-year-old daughter and enjoys entertaining friends.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:21.590
“This is our dining space, with this table
from the fifties drawn by Oswald do Bossani.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:26.310
The chairs are from the same years.”

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:35.519
A narrow staircase, integrated into the shelving unit, leads up to the 9th floor.

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:39.519
This used to be a windowless room that was used as storage space.

00:02:39.519 --> 00:02:44.879
Cornelio replaced the concrete walls with
glass, converting the room into a studio.

00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:55.799
“It's a very special place to stay during
the weekend, or in the evening to look at

00:02:55.799 --> 00:03:03.980
a film or to work, because it is a completely
isolated box.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.139
You can't imagine to be in a town.”

00:03:07.139 --> 00:03:12.859
The studio is almost completely encircled
by an 80 square meter U-shaped terrace.

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:22.199
“You can stay here, reading, working, working
with plants – it’s like to be on holidays.”

00:03:22.199 --> 00:03:27.340
From the terrace you can get to the tenth
floor, which the architect also designed herself.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:30.870
She calls it her sun deck.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:42.459
"When I did the glasshouse I decide to have a roof to use.

00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:45.989
It’s a particular view on the town you never have.

00:03:45.989 --> 00:03:47.519
You feel completely free and you forget what you have to do.”

00:03:47.519 --> 00:03:48.019
Looking out over Milan from this vantage point puts the buildings some considered

00:03:48.019 --> 00:03:48.519
 

00:03:48.519 --> 00:03:51.459
eyesores

00:03:51.459 --> 00:03:52.909
in a whole new light.

